5 0 obj
<</Length 307>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 1 - INTRODUCTION) Tj T*
(This manual applies to every contractor working on company sites.) Tj T*
(It is issued by the Site Safety Office and reviewed every two years.) Tj T*
(Contractors must read it before their first day on site.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
6 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 7 0 R>>
endobj
7 0 obj
<</Length 300>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 2 - SITE INDUCTION) Tj T*
(Every contractor completes a site induction before starting work.) Tj T*
(The induction takes 90 minutes and is valid for twelve months.) Tj T*
(Induction cards must be carried at all times on site.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
8 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 9 0 R>>
endobj
9 0 obj
<</Length 366>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 3 - PERSONAL PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT) Tj T*
(Steel capped boots, a hard hat and safety glasses are required in all work zones.) Tj T*
(Hearing protection is required where noise exceeds 85 decibels.) Tj T*
(Contractors supply their own protective equipment unless the work order says otherwise.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 11 0 R>>
endobj
11 0 obj
<</Length 235>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 4 - SUPERVISION) Tj T*
(Each contractor crew nominates a leading hand before work starts.) Tj T*
(The leading hand is the contact point for the site supervisor.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
12 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 13 0 R>>
endobj
13 0 obj
<</Length 352>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 5 - HOT WORK PERMITS) Tj T*
(Welding, grinding and cutting require a hot work permit.) Tj T*
(A hot work permit is valid for one shift of up to 8 hours.) Tj T*
(Hot work permits are signed off by the duty engineer.) Tj T*
(A fire watch stays for 60 minutes after hot work ends.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
14 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 15 0 R>>
endobj
15 0 obj
<</Length 363>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 6 - CONFINED SPACES) Tj T*
(Entry to a tank, pit or vault requires a confined space permit.) Tj T*
(The atmosphere is tested for oxygen and gas before every entry.) Tj T*
(Confined space permits are signed off by the entry supervisor.) Tj T*
(A confined space permit is valid for 4 hours.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
16 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 17 0 R>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<</Length 319>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 7 - WORKING AT HEIGHTS) Tj T*
(A harness is required for any work above 2 metres without edge protection.) Tj T*
(Harnesses are inspected every six months and tagged.) Tj T*
(Working at heights permits are signed off by the rigging coordinator.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
18 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 19 0 R>>
endobj
19 0 obj
<</Length 284>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 8 - SCAFFOLDING) Tj T*
(Only licensed scaffolders may erect or alter scaffolding.) Tj T*
(Scaffolds are inspected every 30 days and after storms.) Tj T*
(A green scaffold tag means the scaffold is safe to use.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
20 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 21 0 R>>
endobj
21 0 obj
<</Length 282>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 9 - ELECTRICAL ISOLATION) Tj T*
(Equipment is isolated and locked out before maintenance.) Tj T*
(Each worker applies a personal danger lock and tag.) Tj T*
(Only the person who applied a lock may remove it.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
22 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 23 0 R>>
endobj
23 0 obj
<</Length 233>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 10 - PORTABLE ELECTRICAL EQUIPMENT) Tj T*
(Portable tools and leads are tested and tagged every three months.) Tj T*
(Untagged equipment is removed from site.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
24 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 25 0 R>>
endobj
25 0 obj
<</Length 242>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 11 - HAZARDOUS CHEMICALS) Tj T*
(A safety data sheet must be on site for every chemical brought in.) Tj T*
(Chemicals are stored in the bunded store behind Building C.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
26 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 27 0 R>>
endobj
27 0 obj
<</Length 279>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 12 - ASBESTOS) Tj T*
(The asbestos register is held by the Site Safety Office.) Tj T*
(Check the register before drilling or cutting any wall or ceiling.) Tj T*
(Suspected asbestos stops work immediately.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
28 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 29 0 R>>
endobj
29 0 obj
<</Length 305>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 13 - EXCAVATION) Tj T*
(Any dig deeper than 300 millimetres needs a buried services search first.) Tj T*
(Excavation permits are signed off by the civil engineer.) Tj T*
(Trenches deeper than 1.5 metres must be shored or battered.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
30 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 31 0 R>>
endobj
31 0 obj
<</Length 225>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 14 - CRANE LIFTS) Tj T*
(Every crane lift needs a lift plan approved the day before.) Tj T*
(Lifts stop when wind gusts exceed 40 kilometres per hour.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
32 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 33 0 R>>
endobj
33 0 obj
<</Length 309>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 15 - MOBILE PLANT) Tj T*
(Forklifts and elevated work platforms are operated only by licence holders.) Tj T*
(Plant is pre-start checked at the beginning of each shift.) Tj T*
(The site speed limit for plant is 10 kilometres per hour.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
34 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 35 0 R>>
endobj
35 0 obj
<</Length 215>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 16 - TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT) Tj T*
(Pedestrian walkways are marked in yellow and must be kept clear.) Tj T*
(Reversing plant requires a spotter.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
36 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 37 0 R>>
endobj
37 0 obj
<</Length 224>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 17 - NOISE AND VIBRATION) Tj T*
(Noisy work is limited to 7am to 5pm on weekdays.) Tj T*
(Jackhammer use is rotated between workers every 30 minutes.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
38 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 39 0 R>>
endobj
39 0 obj
<</Length 235>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 18 - DUST AND SILICA) Tj T*
(Cutting concrete or stone requires water suppression or on-tool extraction.) Tj T*
(P2 respirators are required during dry cutting.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
40 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 41 0 R>>
endobj
41 0 obj
<</Length 174>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 19 - MANUAL HANDLING) Tj T*
(Loads over 20 kilograms require a two person lift or a mechanical aid.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
42 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 43 0 R>>
endobj
43 0 obj
<</Length 215>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 20 - HOUSEKEEPING) Tj T*
(Work areas are cleaned at the end of every shift.) Tj T*
(Waste is separated into general, metal and timber skips.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
44 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 45 0 R>>
endobj
45 0 obj
<</Length 206>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 21 - FIRST AID) Tj T*
(Each crew of five or more carries a first aid kit.) Tj T*
(The site first aid room is next to the gatehouse.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
46 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 47 0 R>>
endobj
47 0 obj
<</Length 239>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 22 - HEAT STRESS) Tj T*
(When the temperature exceeds 35 degrees, crews take a 10 minute break every hour.) Tj T*
(Cool drinking water is provided at the gatehouse.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
48 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 49 0 R>>
endobj
49 0 obj
<</Length 234>>
stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 730 Td 15 TL
(CONTRACTOR SAFETY MANUAL - SECTION 23 - TEMPORARY LIGHTING) Tj T*
(Temporary lighting must provide at least 160 lux in work areas.) Tj T*
(Lighting leads are run overhead, never across walkways.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
50 0 obj
<</Type/Page/Parent 2 0 R/MediaBox[0 0 612 792]/Resources<</Font<</F1 3 0 R>>>>/Contents 51 0 R>>
endobj
